  "semantics": [
    "Partial charges emit only with one finite source value per atom and a nonempty non-NO_CHARGES source method label. No missing values are filled, no charges are calculated, and no partial charge is rounded into a formal charge.",
    "Reparsed partialCharges values require exact f64 bit equality through verified atom correspondence for preserved status; source method label retention does not verify the method itself.",
    "Parsed trimmed molecule name emits as properties.name and is checked on reparse; original source whitespace remains a declared source_text loss.",
    "New metadata is additive to checked conversion only; legacy graph-only CJSON parsing/writing and immutable CJSON opaque-retention contracts remain unchanged.",
    "Strict cross-format conversion still refuses other losses and unverified chemistry. Fields such as source atom IDs/types/names, substructures and opaque sections are not generally preserved in CJSON."
  ]
